  "scope": "# Review \u2014 `fcac68386147` repeat-offset prototype\nTask/source: generator `2.0.0`, SHA-256 `e3cb70cda6c756fd3124cc0211641e83381f144ccc3245db06653f775236c005`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: the retained test assumed a checkout-relative root and failed in the supported portable runner; it now uses shared root/canonical helpers and normalized semantic Racket comparison.\nPrototype: added proposed `row_repeat_offset` and `column_repeat_offset` values in `{0,1}`, fixed once per episode; `(0,0)` is byte-for-byte canonical.\nAuthority: production `generator.py`, canonical JSONL, and canonical Racket source are unchanged; normalized rule hash remains `350a34d04ac2`.\nFocused checks: final selected-task suite passed **33 tests + 13 subtests**; one pre-existing private-API deprecation warning remains.\nExact Racket evidence: **4 settings, 4 episodes, 3 demos + 4 queries each, 112 outputs checked**, all matching the independent Python mirror.\nTeaching evidence: every declared rival setting was refuted by demonstrations and every one of the four queries distinguished every rival.\nAdversarial pass: **4,096 sampled inputs**, maximum declared boundary output **30\u00d730**, and four exact public/private reconstructions; no bounded finding.\nRemaining scoped failures: none. Production teaching-shortcut findings from the prior audit remain unresolved because production lesson assembly was intentionally unchanged.\nLimits: proposed prototype only; finite declared-rival evidence is not approval, training admission, unique-induction proof, or measured learning benefit.\nAssessment: routine prototype-only extension plus portable-test repair; ready for maintainer replay.",
